(97, 'Hi, Team!\r\n\r\nPlease be informed that the File Request feature on Harley is currently unavailable. If you need to file a leave for today or in the coming days, kindly email HR directly.', 'Harley Leave Request', 'Admin', '2025-08-13 15:48:19', NULL, 0),
(98, 'Good news! Requesting overtime is now simpler. \r\n\r\nYou no longer need a separate OT time in and time out, just clock your time as usual and Harley will do the rest.\r\n\r\nHow it works (step-by-step)\r\n\r\nTime In at your normal start time. \r\n\r\nWork your regular shift as usual.\r\n\r\nIf you’re doing OT, keep working past your regular schedule.\r\n\r\nClock Out when you’re done for the day (including overtime hours).\r\n\r\nHarley will auto-flag the day as OT-eligible if your Time Out is more than 30 minutes after your default end time.\r\n\r\nImportant Rules:\r\n\r\nYou must exceed 30 minutes past your default end time for that day to qualify as OT.\r\nOT requests expire after 5 days, make sure you submit your requests before then.', 'Announcement: New “Harley” Overtime Request UPDATE', 'Admin', '2025-08-14 15:46:07', '[{\"original\":\"1.png\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_689d943f727375.77698651.png\"},{\"original\":\"2.png\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_689d943f72acf7.36919359.png\"}]', 0),
(99, 'Hi, Everyone!\r\n\r\nPlease take a moment to review your attendance logs for the period August 1 to 15 and resolve any issues or discrepancies until 2PM today. This will help us avoid problems during payroll processing.', 'Reminder: Settle Attendance Issues', 'Admin', '2025-08-15 08:19:49', NULL, 1),
(100, 'Hi, Everyone! \r\n\r\nPlease take a moment to review your attendance logs for the period August 1 to 15 and resolve any issues or discrepancies until 12 NOON tomorrow. This will help us avoid problems during payroll processing.', 'Reminder: Settle Attendance Issues (Aug 1–15)', 'Admin', '2025-08-15 15:52:31', NULL, 0),
(101, 'Hi Team, Happy Monday! 🌸\r\n\r\nThis is a reminder regarding the upcoming Philippine holidays:\r\n\r\nAugust 21, 2025 (Thursday) – Special Non-Working Holiday (Ninoy Aquino Day)\r\n- If your client requires you to work, you will receive an additional 30% premium pay.\r\n- If your client does not require you to work and you do not have leave credits, it will be on a no work, no pay basis.\r\n\r\nAugust 25, 2025 (Monday) – Regular/Public Holiday (National Heroes Day)\r\n\r\nFor team members following PH holidays:\r\n• If your client requires you to work, you will receive 100% premium pay.\r\n\r\nFor team members following AU holidays:\r\n• This day will be treated as a regular working day (no additional premium) as this is a matched holiday.\r\n\r\nPlease make sure to secure approval from your client if you will be working on these days. We have also sent a separate email to your clients regarding this.\r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', 'Reminder: Upcoming Philippine Holidays', 'Admin', '2025-08-18 14:45:42', NULL, 0),
(102, 'Good afternoon, Team!\r\n\r\nThe draft payslips will be released today. For those with incomplete logins or late VL/SL filings, please expect corresponding deductions. Kindly review your timelogs, and if you notice any incomplete entries, please file a time adjustment or VL/SL request so we can apply the necessary changes to the final draft.\r\n\r\nIf no time adjustment or VL/SL is filed, we unfortunately won’t be able to make any corrections. \r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', 'Reminder: Review Your Timelogs for Payslip Adjustments', 'Admin', '2025-08-19 12:51:05', NULL, 0),
(103, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nPlease be advised that your salaries for August 1–15 have been credited yesterday.\r\nFor any disputes, kindly send an email with the subject line: Dispute.', 'August 1–15 Salary Update', 'Admin', '2025-08-21 06:55:36', NULL, 0),
(104, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nPlease be informed that there will be a scheduled power outage on Sunday, August 24, 2025, as part of the ATS Preventive Maintenance.\r\n\r\nEmployees present in the office may experience temporary interruptions lasting 5–10 minutes around the following times:\r\n* 1:00 PM\r\n* 1:40 PM\r\n* 3:10 PM\r\n\r\nNote: The times above are only estimates. Outages may occur slightly earlier or later than scheduled.\r\n\r\nAs a precaution, kindly ensure that you:\r\n* Save your work regularly\r\n* Enable the auto-save feature for files and applications\r\n* Secure any backup files in advance\r\n\r\nThank you for your cooperation and understanding.', 'Subject: Scheduled Power Interruption – ATS Preventive Maintenance (August 24, 2025)', 'Admin', '2025-08-23 19:35:49', NULL, 0),
(105, 'Hi Everyone,\r\n\r\nPlease be informed that the SSS Employer’s Portal is currently down. For those with pending loan applications, kindly allow us until tomorrow to process them.\r\n\r\nThank you for your understanding!\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', 'SSS Employer’s Portal Downtime', 'Admin', '2025-08-25 09:55:21', '[{\"original\":\"Screenshot 2025-08-25 095500.png\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68abc289e62a52.42524612.png\"}]', 0),
(106, 'Hi Team,\r\n \r\nPlease do not update your PCs with the August 2025 Windows 11 (Version 24H2) security update (KB5063878) until further notice.\r\n \r\nMicrosoft has confirmed multiple critical issues with this update, including:\r\n \r\nSSD/HDD Failure & Data Loss – Drives may disappear or become corrupted after large file transfers.\r\n \r\nStreaming & Performance Problems – Applications like OBS or NDI may experience severe lag.\r\n \r\nSystem Recovery Issues – Certain recovery functions may fail after installation (some builds).\r\n \r\nWhat You Need to Do\r\n \r\nPause Windows Updates temporarily.\r\n \r\nDo not manually install the latest cumulative update.\r\n \r\nWait for IT to confirm when it is safe to update.\r\n \r\nWhy This Matters\r\n \r\nInstalling the update may result in data loss, system instability, or downtime.\r\n \r\nThank you for your cooperation.\r\n \r\nRegards,\r\nIT Department', 'Warning: Windows 11 August Update Causing System & SSD Issues', 'Admin', '2025-08-25 09:59:10', '[{\"original\":\"Media.png\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68abc36e612777.63230789.png\"}]', 0),
(107, 'Hi All, \r\n\r\nHappy Thursday!\r\n\r\nAs our enrollment with our HMO partner is ongoing, we would like to ask team members who wish to enroll an additional dependent (on top of your FREE dependent) to accomplish the HMO Enrollment Form below and complete the attached Authority to Deduct (ATD).\r\n\r\nPlease note that if you add an additional dependent, you will shoulder 100% of the cost. We are billed on a bi-yearly basis, which means you will need to pay the 6 months upfront (August 2025 – February 2026).\r\n\r\nLink: https://forms.office.com/r/kqUvSkPkTF\r\n\r\nIf you wish to proceed, kindly accomplish the form and email the signed ATD to HR@resourcestaff.com.ph on or before August 29, 2025 (Friday) by 1:00 PM.\r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nHR Department', 'HMO Enrollment – Additional Dependent Registration', 'Admin', '2025-08-28 08:54:26', '[{\"original\":\"Authority to Deduct - HMO.pdf\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68afa8c2121636.32900812.pdf\"}]', 0),
(108, 'Hi All,\r\n\r\nWe’re inviting everyone to join our Engagement Thursday today at 1:00 PM! 🎉\r\n\r\nLet’s take this time to catch up on company updates and enjoy some good food and drinks together.\r\n\r\n📍 Pantry – 1:00 PM\r\n\r\nSee you there!\r\n\r\nCheers, \r\nHR Department', 'Engagement Thursday', 'Admin', '2025-08-28 11:27:34', NULL, 0),
(109, 'Hi Everyone,\r\n\r\nHappy Friday!\r\n\r\nCongratulations once again to all the winners of our game and the Best Attendance Award! 🎉 Kindly visit the HR office to claim your prize.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', 'Engagement Thursday', 'Admin', '2025-08-29 07:45:26', NULL, 0),
(110, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nWe hope you are all safe and dry. Please be informed that light to moderate rains are currently affecting Pampanga (Arayat, Candaba, Santa Ana, San Luis, San Simon, Santo Tomas, Minalin, Magalang, Apalit) and nearby provinces due to the Southwest Monsoon (Habagat) and a Low Pressure Area (LPA).\r\n\r\nFor your safety, please stay vigilant and monitor weather updates.\r\n\r\nIf you are experiencing difficulty getting to work due to the weather, kindly inform your supervisor as soon as possible through email, chat, or your usual communication channel.\r\n\r\nFor comfort, you may dress down temporarily, provided you bring spare clothes to change into once you arrive at the office.\r\n\r\nIn case of emergency, please contact:\r\n- Angeles City: 0917-851-9581 / 0998-842-7746\r\n- City of San Fernando (CSFP): 0939-936-2423 / 0939-961-4357\r\n- Mabalacat City: 0998-999-4357\r\n\r\nYour safety is our priority. Thank you and please stay safe!\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nHR Department', '📢 Weather Advisory: September 1, 2025 (Monday)', 'Admin', '2025-09-01 09:29:58', NULL, 0),
(111, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nWe hope you are all safe and dry.\r\n\r\nAccording to PAGASA’s advisory at 6:47 a.m., moderate to heavy rainshowers with lightning and strong winds are expected over Metro Manila, Cavite, Pampanga, Bataan, Rizal, Quezon, and Zambales within the next two hours.\r\n\r\n👉 For your safety, please stay vigilant and continue monitoring weather updates.\r\n👉 If you are experiencing difficulty getting to work due to the weather, kindly inform your supervisor as soon as possible through email, chat, or your usual communication channel.\r\n👉 For comfort, you may dress down temporarily, provided you bring spare clothes to change into once you arrive at the office.\r\n\r\n📞 Emergency hotlines:\r\n\r\n- Angeles City: 0917-851-9581 / 0998-842-7746\r\n- City of San Fernando (CSFP): 0939-936-2423 / 0939-961-4357\r\n- Mabalacat City: 0998-999-4357\r\n\r\nYour safety is our priority. Please take care and stay safe!\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nHR Department', '📢 Weather Advisory: September 2, 2025 (Wednesday)', 'Admin', '2025-09-03 06:57:54', NULL, 1),
(112, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nWe hope you are all safe and dry.\r\n\r\nAccording to PAGASA’s advisory at 6:47 a.m., moderate to heavy rainshowers with lightning and strong winds are expected over Metro Manila, Cavite, Pampanga, Bataan, Rizal, Quezon, and Zambales within the next two hours.\r\n\r\n👉 For your safety, please stay vigilant and continue monitoring weather updates.\r\n👉 If you are experiencing difficulty getting to work due to the weather, kindly inform your supervisor as soon as possible through email, chat, or your usual communication channel.\r\n👉 For comfort, you may dress down temporarily, provided you bring spare clothes to change into once you arrive at the office.\r\n\r\n📞 Emergency hotlines:\r\n\r\n- Angeles City: 0917-851-9581 / 0998-842-7746\r\n- City of San Fernando (CSFP): 0939-936-2423 / 0939-961-4357\r\n- Mabalacat City: 0998-999-4357\r\n\r\nYour safety is our priority. Please take care and stay safe!\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nHR Department', '📢 Weather Advisory: September 3, 2025 (Wednesday)', 'Admin', '2025-09-03 06:58:40', NULL, 0),
(113, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nHappy Hump Day!\r\n\r\nThe draft payslips will be released today. For those with incomplete logins or late VL/SL filings, please expect corresponding deductions. Kindly review your timelogs, and if you notice any incomplete entries, please file a time adjustment or VL/SL request on or before 2 PM today so we can apply the necessary changes to the final draft.\r\n\r\nIf no time adjustment or VL/SL is filed, we unfortunately won’t be able to make any corrections.\r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', 'Reminder: Review Your Timelogs for Payslip Adjustments', 'Admin', '2025-09-03 09:10:10', NULL, 0),
(114, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nIf you have any concerns regarding the September 5, 2025 Payout, please send an email to hr@resourcestaff.com.ph and copy rica.tolomia@resourcestaff.com.ph. Use the subject line: PAYROLL CONCERN: September 5, 2025 Payout.\r\n\r\nKindly include:\r\n\r\n- A screenshot of your payslip\r\n- Any adjustments/requests filed in Harley\r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', 'PAYROLL QUERY: September 5, 2025 Payout', 'Admin', '2025-09-03 09:23:15', NULL, 0),
(115, 'Hi All,\r\n\r\nHappy Friday!\r\n\r\nIt has been brought to our attention that some team members encountered login issues this morning, September 5, 2025, between 6:30 AM and 8:00 AM. The issue has now been resolved, and you should be able to clock in and out as normal.\r\n\r\nWe encourage everyone to review their timelog records and file any necessary time adjustments. Please don’t hesitate to reach out if you need further assistance.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', 'Timekeeping System Update', 'Admin', '2025-09-05 09:04:41', '[{\"original\":\"Timelogs.png\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68ba37295feb35.16432642.png\"}]', 0),
(116, 'PAGASA, in its 11:00 AM bulletin, has issued a Yellow Rainfall Warning for the following areas:\r\n\r\nZambales\r\n\r\nBataan\r\n\r\nTarlac (San Jose, Capas, Bamban)\r\n\r\nPampanga (Porac, Floridablanca)\r\n\r\nLight to moderate rains are expected in the next few hours. Residents in low-lying and flood-prone areas are advised to remain alert as flooding is possible.\r\n\r\n📞 Emergency hotlines:\r\n\r\n- Angeles City: 0917-851-9581 / 0998-842-7746\r\n- City of San Fernando (CSFP): 0939-936-2423 / 0939-961-4357\r\n- Mabalacat City: 0998-999-4357\r\n\r\nYour safety is our priority. Please take care and stay safe!\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nHR Departmen', '🌧️ Weather Advisory – Friday, September 5, 2025', 'Admin', '2025-09-05 12:07:24', NULL, 0),
(117, 'Hi All,\r\n\r\nWe’re glad to inform you that salaries have already been credited to your accounts. \r\n\r\nHave a great weekend ahead!', 'Payroll: Aug 16 - 31, 2025', 'Admin', '2025-09-05 12:44:33', NULL, 0),
(118, 'Hi All,\r\n\r\nThe salaries have now been credited to your accounts.', 'Payroll: Aug 16 -31, 2025', 'Admin', '2025-09-05 13:04:08', NULL, 1),
(119, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nWe have been informed that there will be building maintenance, and the elevators will be unavailable from approximately 2:00 PM to 3:00 PM. Kindly use the stairs during this time.\r\n\r\nThank you for your understanding!\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nFacilities', 'Temporary Elevator Unavailability – Building Maintenance', 'Admin', '2025-09-05 14:08:39', NULL, 0),
(120, 'May I kindly ask if any team member owns a vehicle with the plate number CKH 548? If so, we would appreciate it if you could move the car to a designated parking space at the soonest possible time.\r\n\r\nThank you for your cooperation.\r\n\r\nBest regards,\r\nHR Department', 'Request to Move Vehicle', 'Admin', '2025-09-10 08:04:14', NULL, 0),
(121, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nAt 2:09 PM today, an estimated magnitude 4.3 earthquake was recorded 61 km from Olongapo City, Zambales. While no immediate damage has been reported in our area, please stay alert and follow safety precautions.\r\n\r\nSafety Reminders:\r\n\r\n✅ Stay vigilant and be mindful of possible aftershocks.\r\n✅ Check your surroundings for any hazards or damages.\r\n\r\nYour safety remains our top priority. Please report any concerns to the Admin/HR team immediately.\r\n\r\nStay safe, everyone! 🙏\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nHR Department', '📢 Advisory: Earthquake Safety Reminder', 'Admin', '2025-09-11 14:17:05', NULL, 0),
(122, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nPlease be informed of a scheduled power interruption from Clark Electric on Sunday, September 14, during the following periods:\r\n\r\n- 7:00 AM to 7:30 AM\r\n- 1:00 PM to 1:30 PM\r\n\r\nThis temporary outage is necessary to facilitate the rerouting of the KS-02 and KS-07 feeders.\r\n\r\nThe generator will run to avoid any delay in our operations. However, we encourage everyone to save their files and work regularly to prevent any data loss.\r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nFacilities', 'September 14, 2025 (Sunday) Interruption Notice', 'Admin', '2025-09-12 16:17:50', NULL, 0),
(123, 'Hi All,\r\n\r\nAs we prepare for the upcoming September 20 payout, please check your Harley logs and file any necessary time adjustments. Kindly ensure that all adjustments, overtime, change of schedule, and leave requests are filed on or before September 16, 2025, at 1:00 PM.\r\n\r\nPlease note that any late filings will be credited on the next payout.\r\n\r\nIf you encounter any system errors, kindly email Cedrick.Arnigo@resourcestaff.com.ph and copy HR, using the subject line: Harley Query.\r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nHR Department', 'Reminder: Timekeeping Adjustments for September 20 Payout', 'Admin', '2025-09-12 16:21:59', NULL, 0),
(124, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nHappy Friday!\r\n\r\nMSN. :)\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', 'September 20 Payout', 'Admin', '2025-09-19 14:33:37', NULL, 0),
(125, 'Please be advised that we will be reviewing your leave credits to ensure their accuracy. \r\n\r\nThank you for your attention to this matter.', 'Harley Advisory: Leave Credits', 'Admin', '2025-09-19 15:55:10', NULL, 0),
(126, 'Hi All,\r\n\r\nPAGASA has issued a Heavy Rainfall Warning as of 9:30 AM today:\r\n\r\n🔶 Orange Rainfall Warning: Zambales\r\n🟡 Yellow Rainfall Warning: Tarlac, Pampanga, Bulacan, Bataan, Metro Manila, Rizal, Batangas, and Cavite\r\n\r\nPlease be vigilant and take necessary precautions, especially in flood-prone areas.\r\n\r\n📞 Emergency Hotlines:\r\n\r\nAngeles City: 0917-851-9581 / 0998-842-7746\r\n\r\nCity of San Fernando (CSFP): 0939-936-2423 / 0939-961-4357\r\n\r\nMabalacat City: 0998-999-4357\r\n\r\nYour safety is our top priority. Stay indoors if possible, monitor local advisories, and don\'t hesitate to contact the emergency lines if needed.\r\n\r\nTake care and stay safe!\r\n\r\nBest regards,\r\nHR Department', '🌧️ Weather Advisory – Monday, September 22, 2025', 'Admin', '2025-09-22 10:25:23', NULL, 0),
(127, 'Hi all,\r\n\r\nI hope everyone is safe and sound. Pampanga is currently under an orange warning due to super typhoon Nando. An advisory has already been sent to your client.\r\n\r\nYour safety is our number one priority. If you need any assistance, please reach out to the HR hotline below:\r\n\r\n- 09190993036\r\n- 09150561780\r\n- 09982971494\r\n\r\nThank you and stay safe!', '🌧️ Weather Advisory – Monday, September 22, 2025', 'Admin', '2025-09-22 19:15:31', NULL, 0),
(128, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nWe are excited to invite everyone to join our Engagement Thursday tomorrow, September 25, 2025. In line with Suicide Prevention Month, we will be holding a seminar focused on awareness, support, and prevention strategies.\r\n\r\n📌 Program Proper\r\n\r\n12:00 NN – HR Presentation and Announcement, Games, and Food\r\n1:00 PM – 2:00 PM – Suicide Prevention Webinar\r\n\r\n🔗 Webinar Link: [Please see QR below]\r\n\r\nThis is a meaningful opportunity to learn how we can take care of our own mental health and support others in need. Your participation will help us create a safer and more compassionate workplace.\r\n\r\nWe look forward to seeing you all there!\r\n\r\nBest regards,\r\nHR Department', 'Suicide Prevention Month Seminar – September 25, 2025', 'Admin', '2025-09-24 15:49:13', '[{\"original\":\"qr-code.png\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68d3a27935fc05.37578156.png\"}]', 0),
(129, 'Hi Team, \r\n\r\nHappy Tuesday!\r\n\r\nJust a reminder to all team members to file your OTs, Leaves, Time Adjustments, and Change Working Schedule in Harley on or before 9:00 AM tomorrow, October 1, 2025.\r\n\r\nWe will be endorsing the timekeeping report for payroll processing at 9:30 AM sharp tomorrow. Any late filings will be processed in the next cutoff.\r\n\r\nPlease ensure to double-check your time logs today and reach out if you encounter any system errors.\r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', 'Reminder: Deadline for Filing in Harley', 'Admin', '2025-09-30 08:07:30', NULL, 0),
(130, '📺👻 Hey Team! \r\n\r\nThis Halloween, RSS 2025 is turning into a Netflix Nightmare! 🎃 Get ready for thrills, chills, and plenty of fun as we bring to life spooky spins on our favorite Netflix shows and movies—Stranger Things, Squid Game, Wednesday, and more! 🌟 \r\n\r\nSo, what’s on the agenda? We’ve got some exciting activities lined up: \r\n\r\n🎨 Best Bay Design \r\nTransform your bays into eerie Netflix scenes! Whether it’s the Upside Down from Stranger Things, the haunting halls of Wednesday Addams’ Academy, or a chilling Squid Game arena, let your creativity shine as you design the ultimate nightmare set. \r\n\r\n📌 Registration Required: \r\n\r\nGroups must register. \r\nRegistration Deadline: October 20, 2025 \r\nSubmit via HR’s Microsoft Form  \r\nOnly registered groups will be eligible for judging and prizes. \r\n\r\n🎭 Best Costume Design (Employees & Kids) \r\nStep into the spotlight as your favorite Netflix character! Go solo or help your kids shine in the parade, it’s your time to scare, amuse, or wow the crowd. \r\n\r\nEmployee Prizes: \r\n\r\nScariest Costume – ₱5,000 \r\nFunniest Costume – ₱3,000 \r\nMost Creative Costume – ₱1,000 \r\n\r\nKids Prizes: \r\nCutest Costume – Gift Pack ₱2,000 \r\nSpookiest Costume – Gift Pack ₱2,000 \r\nMost Creative Costume – Gift Pack ₱2,000 \r\n\r\n🖥️ Best WFH Station Design \r\nWFH warriors, show us your haunted Netflix setups! From a creepy Bridgerton tea corner to a Witcher monster hunt scene, bring the Halloween vibe right to your desk. \r\n\r\nPrizes: \r\n\r\nWinner – ₱3,000 Voucher \r\nRunner-Up – ₱2,000 Voucher \r\nThird Place – ₱1,000 Voucher \r\n\r\n🍬 Trick or Treat Fun! 🍬 \r\nStarting at 1:15 PM, kids will make their way through Netflix-inspired bays to collect candies! 🎃 \r\n\r\nRegistration Details: \r\n\r\nDates: Opens Oct 8 (2:00 PM) – Closes Oct 25 (12:00 PM) \r\nMax Kids: Up to 3 children per employee (ages 0–10) \r\nTo Register: Fill out HR’s Microsoft Form \r\n\r\nNote: Only pre-registered kids may join Trick-or-Treat and Kids’ Costume Awards', 'Stream & Scream: Your Halloween Binge Begins!', 'Admin', '2025-09-30 18:16:16', NULL, 1),
(131, '📺👻 Hey Team!\r\n\r\nThis Halloween, RSS 2025 is turning into a Netflix Nightmare! 🎃 Get ready for thrills, chills, and plenty of fun as we bring to life spooky spins on our favorite Netflix shows and movies—Stranger Things, Squid Game, Wednesday, and more! 🌟\r\n\r\nSo, what’s on the agenda? We’ve got some exciting activities lined up:\r\n\r\n🎨 Best Bay Design\r\nTransform your bays into eerie Netflix scenes! Whether it’s the Upside Down from Stranger Things, the haunting halls of Wednesday Addams’ Academy, or a chilling Squid Game arena, let your creativity shine as you design the ultimate nightmare set.\r\n\r\n📌 Registration Required:\r\n\r\nGroups must register.\r\nRegistration Deadline: October 20, 2025\r\nSubmit via HR’s Microsoft Form\r\nOnly registered groups will be eligible for judging and prizes.\r\n\r\n🎭 Best Costume Design (Employees & Kids)\r\nStep into the spotlight as your favorite Netflix character! Go solo or help your kids shine in the parade, it’s your time to scare, amuse, or wow the crowd.\r\n\r\nEmployee Prizes:\r\n\r\nScariest Costume – ₱5,000\r\nFunniest Costume – ₱3,000\r\nMost Creative Costume – ₱1,000\r\n\r\nKids Prizes:\r\nCutest Costume – Gift Pack ₱2,000\r\nSpookiest Costume – Gift Pack ₱2,000\r\nMost Creative Costume – Gift Pack ₱2,000\r\n\r\n🖥️ Best WFH Station Design\r\nWFH warriors, show us your haunted Netflix setups! From a creepy Bridgerton tea corner to a Witcher monster hunt scene, bring the Halloween vibe right to your desk.\r\n\r\nPrizes:\r\n\r\nWinner – ₱3,000 Voucher\r\nRunner-Up – ₱2,000 Voucher\r\nThird Place – ₱1,000 Voucher\r\n\r\n🍬 Trick or Treat Fun! 🍬\r\nStarting at 1:15 PM, kids will make their way through Netflix-inspired bays to collect candies! 🎃\r\n\r\nRegistration Details:\r\n\r\nDates: Opens Oct 8 (2:00 PM) – Closes Oct 25 (12:00 PM)\r\nMax Kids: Up to 3 children per employee (ages 0–10)\r\nTo Register: Fill out HR’s Microsoft Form\r\n\r\nNote: Only pre-registered kids may join Trick-or-Treat and Kids’ Costume Awards', 'Stream & Scream: Your Halloween Binge Begins!', 'Admin', '2025-09-30 18:17:22', '[{\"original\":\"Engagement Thursday.png\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68dbae32edee58.07942244.png\"}]', 0),
(132, 'Hi All,\r\n\r\nPlease see below the QR code for the Bay Design Registration Form. Kindly be reminded that only the group representative should accomplish and submit the form on behalf of the team.\r\n\r\nThe form will be available until October 20, 2025, at 12:00 PM. Please note that only registered groups will be eligible for judging.\r\n\r\nShould you have any questions, feel free to reach out.', 'Group Registration Form: Bay Design Contest', 'Admin', '2025-10-06 09:06:59', '[{\"original\":\"GROUP.jpg\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68e31633aae182.61169024.jpg\"}]', 0),
(133, 'i Team,\r\n\r\nPlease be informed that as of 10/6/2025, leave credits are temporarily unavailable. All leave credits have been set to 0 for the time being and leave restrictions have been lifted until further notice. Employees can file leave as usual.\r\n\r\nIf you have any more concerns kindly send an email to the HR.', 'Advisory Regarding Leave Credits', 'Admin', '2025-10-06 16:04:28', NULL, 1),
(134, 'Hi Team,\r\n\r\nPlease be informed that as of 10/6/2025, leave credits are temporarily unavailable. All leave credits have been set to 0 for the time being and leave restrictions have been lifted until further notice. Employees can file leave as usual.\r\n\r\nIf you have any more concerns kindly send an email to the HR', 'Advisory Regarding Leave Credits', 'Admin', '2025-10-06 16:04:44', NULL, 0),
(135, 'The wait is over — registration for RSS 2025: Netflix Nightmare is officially OPEN! 😱🍿\r\n\r\nHave you registered your group yet? Don’t miss out on the frightful fun, spooky prizes, and hauntingly creative competitions! Check out the details below 👇\r\n\r\n\r\n🎨  BEST BAY DESIGN (Registration Required)\r\n\r\n• Form your group and register by scanning the QR code below.\r\n• Nominate one (1) group representative.\r\n• Deadline: 🗓️ October 20, 2025\r\n• Submit via HR’s Microsoft Form.\r\n• Only registered groups are eligible for judging and prizes.\r\n\r\n \r\n🎯 Judging Criteria (30/20 System)\r\n\r\n👻 Kids’ Votes (50%) – Each child will receive two stickers: one worth 30 points (top choice) and one worth 20 points (second choice).\r\n🧛 Group Representative Votes (50%) – Each team rep gets two votes: one worth 30 points and one worth 20 points (you can’t vote for your own team!).\r\nFinal Score = Kids’ Score (50) + Team Representative Score (50)\r\n\r\n\r\n🏆 Prizes\r\n\r\n🥇 Winner – ₱10,000\r\n🥈 1st Runner-Up – ₱8,000\r\n🥉 2nd Runner-Up – ₱3,000\r\n\r\n \r\n🖥️ BEST WFH STATION DESIGN\r\n\r\nCalling all WFH warriors! 💻 Show us your haunted Netflix setups! Whether it’s a spooky Bridgerton tea corner or a Witcher monster lair, bring the Halloween chills right to your desk!\r\n\r\n🏆 Prizes\r\n\r\n🥇 Winner – ₱3,000 Voucher\r\n🥈 Runner-Up – ₱2,000 Voucher\r\n🥉 Third Place – ₱1,000 Voucher\r\n\r\n \r\n🎯 Judging Criteria (100%)\r\n\r\n• Creativity & Originality – 40%\r\n• Halloween Vibe – 30%\r\n• Effort & Details – 20%\r\n• Presentation – 10%\r\n\r\n \r\n🎭 BEST COSTUME DESIGN (Employees & Kids)\r\n\r\nGet your costumes ready — it’s time to slay the runway! 😈\r\n\r\n\r\n👔 Employee Prizes\r\n\r\n• Scariest Costume – ₱5,000\r\n• Funniest Costume – ₱3,000\r\n• Most Creative Costume – ₱1,000\r\n\r\n \r\n🧒 Kids Prizes\r\n\r\n• Cutest Costume – Gift Pack worth ₱2,000\r\n• Spookiest Costume – Gift Pack worth ₱2,000\r\n• Most Creative Costume – Gift Pack worth ₱2,000\r\n\r\n \r\n🎯 Judging Criteria\r\n\r\n• Creativity & Originality – 40%\r\n• Accuracy / Vibe – 30%\r\n• Stage Presence / Effort – 20%\r\n• Audience Impact – 10%\r\n\r\nSo, what are you waiting for? Grab your teammates, unleash your inner artist, and get ready to turn Netflix nightmares into spooktacular masterpieces! 👻✨\r\n \r\nCheers,\r\nHR Department', '👻 It’s Showtime! Join RSS 2025: Netflix Nightmare — Register Now!', 'Admin', '2025-10-07 15:04:14', '[{\"original\":\"GROUP.jpg\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68e4bb6e6317f5.64271151.jpg\"}]', 0),
(136, 'Hi there, registration for RSS 2025: Netflix Nightmare Trick-or-Treat is now OPEN! 😱🍿\r\n\r\nGet your little stars ready for an afternoon full of fun, candies, games, and Halloween magic! 🧙‍♀️✨\r\n\r\n🍬 Trick-or-Treat Fun! 🍬\r\nStarting at 1:15 PM, kids will go on a Netflix-themed adventure, visiting different bays to collect candies and treats! 🎃\r\n\r\nRegistration Details:\r\n📅 Opens: October 8 (2:00 PM)\r\n⏰ Closes: October 25 (12:00 PM)\r\n👧🧒 Who Can Join: Up to 3 children per employee (ages 0–10)\r\n📝 How to Register: Scan the QR code provided by HR to register your kids!\r\n⚠️ Important: Only pre-registered kids can join the Trick-or-Treat and Kids’ Costume Awards.\r\n🕒 Program Schedule (1:00 PM – 4:00 PM)\r\n1:00 – 1:15 PM → Opening & Welcome\r\n1:15 – 2:00 PM → Trick-or-Treat Walkthrough 🍭\r\n2:00 – 2:30 PM → Team Games & Fun Segment 🎯\r\n2:30 – 3:15 PM → Costume Parade & Judging 🧛‍♀️\r\n3:15 – 3:45 PM → Awarding Ceremony 🏆\r\n3:45 – 4:00 PM → Closing & Group Photo 📸\r\n\r\n✨ Let’s Make This a Spook-tacular Netflix Halloween! ✨\r\n\r\nDress up your little ones as their favorite Netflix characters, bring their candy bags, and get ready for an afternoon of smiles, laughter, and treats galore!\r\nWe can’t wait to see all the adorable costumes and spooky fun at RSS Netflix Nightmare 2025! 👻🎬🍬', '🎬 RSS Bulletin: Netflix Nightmare 2025 – Trick-or-Treat for the Kids! 👻', 'Admin', '2025-10-09 12:35:26', '[{\"original\":\"Kids.png\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68e73b8e15ab46.57012006.png\"}]', 1),
(137, 'A magnitude 5.0 earthquake was felt in Zambales and nearby areas, including Pampanga.\r\n\r\nIf you are indoors when an earthquake happens during  the shaking:\r\n• Duck down to protect yourself from falling objects.\r\n• Cover under a sturdy table or desk to shield yourself from debris.\r\n• Hold on to a sturdy piece of furniture to keep it over you.\r\n\r\nStay inside until the shaking stops. Do not run outside during the earthquake.\r\n\r\nStay away from:\r\n• Windows, glass, and mirrors (to avoid shattering glass).\r\n• Bookshelves, cabinets, and other tall furniture that might fall.\r\n• Kitchens and areas with hanging or heavy objects that can drop.\r\n\r\n\r\nEmergency Hotline (CDC ):\r\n#1232/ #1CDC\r\n0968-6812-437\r\n045 599 3238\r\n045 599 2138\r\n045 499 4357', '⚠️ Earthquake Safety Reminder', 'Admin', '2025-10-11 19:33:00', NULL, 0),
(138, 'A magnitude 5.0 earthquake was felt in Zambales and nearby areas, including Pampanga.\r\n\r\nIf you are indoors when an earthquake happens during  the shaking:\r\n• Duck down to protect yourself from falling objects.\r\n• Cover under a sturdy table or desk to shield yourself from debris.\r\n• Hold on to a sturdy piece of furniture to keep it over you.\r\n\r\nStay inside until the shaking stops. Do not run outside during the earthquake.\r\n\r\nStay away from:\r\n• Windows, glass, and mirrors (to avoid shattering glass).\r\n• Bookshelves, cabinets, and other tall furniture that might fall.\r\n• Kitchens and areas with hanging or heavy objects that can drop.\r\n\r\n\r\nEmergency Hotline (CDC ):\r\n#1232/ #1CDC\r\n0968-6812-437\r\n045 599 3238\r\n045 599 2138\r\n045 499 4357', '⚠️ Earthquake Safety Reminder', 'Admin', '2025-10-11 19:33:01', NULL, 0),
(139, 'Hi there, registration for RSS 2025: Netflix Nightmare Trick-or-Treat is now OPEN! 😱🍿\r\n\r\nGet your little stars ready for an afternoon full of fun, candies, games, and Halloween magic! 🧙‍♀️✨\r\n\r\n🍬 Trick-or-Treat Fun! 🍬\r\nStarting at 1:15 PM, kids will go on a Netflix-themed adventure, visiting different bays to collect candies and treats! 🎃\r\n\r\nRegistration Details:\r\n📅 Opens: October 8 (2:00 PM)\r\n⏰ Closes: October 25 (12:00 PM)\r\n👧🧒 Who Can Join: Up to 3 children per employee (ages 0–10)\r\n📝 How to Register: Scan the QR code provided by HR to register your kids!\r\n⚠️ Important: Only pre-registered kids can join the Trick-or-Treat and Kids’ Costume Awards.\r\n🕒 Program Schedule (1:00 PM – 4:00 PM)\r\n1:00 – 1:15 PM → Opening & Welcome\r\n1:15 – 2:00 PM → Trick-or-Treat Walkthrough 🍭\r\n2:00 – 2:30 PM → Team Games & Fun Segment 🎯\r\n2:30 – 3:15 PM → Costume Parade & Judging 🧛‍♀️\r\n3:15 – 3:45 PM → Awarding Ceremony 🏆\r\n3:45 – 4:00 PM → Closing & Group Photo 📸\r\n\r\n✨ Let’s Make This a Spook-tacular Netflix Halloween! ✨\r\n\r\nDress up your little ones as their favorite Netflix characters, bring their candy bags, and get ready for an afternoon of smiles, laughter, and treats galore!\r\nWe can’t wait to see all the adorable costumes and spooky fun at RSS Netflix Nightmare 2025! 👻🎬🍬', '🎬 RSS Bulletin: Netflix Nightmare 2025 – Trick-or-Treat for the Kids! 👻', 'Admin', '2025-10-14 07:43:05', '[{\"original\":\"Kids (2).png\",\"stored\":\"uploads\\/file_68ed8e897e9c58.25800955.png\"}]', 1);

